      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The dissent's interpretation of the Fourteenth Amendment is fundamentally flawed because it attempts to impose a broad, subjective policy preference onto the text, rather than adhering to established constitutional doctrine. Their argument essentially requires the Court to create a new right not explicitly enumerated, which is an act of judicial legislation, not interpretation. This expansive reading ignores the historical context and the original public meaning of the amendment, rendering their legal reasoning an illegitimate departure from textualism.",
      "source": "target",
