    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for that. i want to be really thorough in my paper though. i'm trying to address the counter-argument that \"liberty\" should be interpreted dynamically to reflect modern standards. when you say their approach is an \"illegitimate departure\" from doctrine, are you saying there's actually no legitimate legal basis for their view at all? as in, is it just a philosophical mistake rather than a valid legal theory that can be debated on technical grounds?",
